# URL Shortener

A URL shortener built with Java Spring Boot, PostgreSQL and Redis.

## Features
- Create short links (Base62 encoding of the database ID, so no collisions)
- 302 redirect to the original URL
- Redis cache-aside with a 1-hour TTL (falls back to Postgres if Redis is down)
- Click analytics per link
- Input validation and clean 400/404 error responses

## Tech stack
Java 17, Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA, PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7, Docker Compose

## Run locally
1. Start the database and cache: `docker compose up -d`
2. Start the app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run`
3. Create a link: `POST http://localhost:8080/api/urls` with `{"longUrl":"https://example.com"}`
4. Open the returned short URL in the browser

## API
| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/urls | Create a short link |
| GET | /{code} | Redirect to the original URL |
| GET | /api/urls/{code}/stats | Click count and details |
